# Personal Incarnation: "{0}: The next 1 damage that would be dealt to this creature this turn is dealt to its owner
# instead" (CR 614.1a, 614.9, 616.1f) and "When this creature dies, its owner loses half their life, rounded up" (CR 119.3,
# 107.1a). Bot1 (starting at 22) activates it once on turn 1, off an empty pool: that effect ends with the turn, so Bot2's
# first Lightning Bolt on turn 2 deals all 3 to the Incarnation. Bot1 then activates it three times. Bot2's Shock to Bot1
# is not damage to the Incarnation and leaves them waiting. They apply one after another to Bot2's second Bolt, 1 each,
# the last to the 1 damage the others left, so all 3 are dealt to Bot1 and none to the Incarnation. They are then used
# up: the third Bolt, in the end step, deals all 3 to it again. With 6 damage it dies, and Bot1, at 17, loses 9.

